/* ===== PASHTO LANGUAGE PACK (Zones 1–8 · early access) =====
   Pashto-DRIVEN curriculum, researched before shipping (Wikipedia Pashto
   alphabet/grammar, Wikivoyage Pashto phrasebook, Omniglot, LingDocs).
   PASHTO IS RIGHT-TO-LEFT — index.html carries an RTL pass keyed on
   :root[data-lang="ps"] (word-bank answer/bank rows, fill sentences and
   big displays flow rtl; each tile is a single text run so nothing else
   needs flipping).
   Romanization scheme (ASCII only, enforced — NO Arabic script in rom
   fields; scan [؀-ۿ]):
   - schwa (zwarakay ə) is written "a" — the de-facto ASCII convention
     (manana, za, yam); long alif = "aa". Vowels: a aa i ee u o e(ې) ay(ی)
     ey(ۍ/ئ). ي inside words = "ee" (دي dee).
   - retroflexes are DOUBLED: ټ tt, ډ dd, ړ rr, ڼ nn (ddoddey, sarray).
   - څ = ts, ځ = dz; خ = kh, غ = gh, ش = sh, ژ = zh, چ = ch, ج = j, ق = q.
   - ښ = x — THE Pashto letter; its sound varies by region (kh in the
     north-east, sh in the south-west) — noted in lessons, audio leads.
   - ږ = g in the course voice (north-east value; zh in the south-west).
   - ع is not written (silent for learners); ح = h, ف = f.
   Grammar spine (what makes Pashto its own thing, and drives the zones):
   SOV word order; two GENDERS with agreeing adjectives (adjective BEFORE
   the noun); the present equative paradigm یم یې دی ده یو یاست دي; present
   verb endings -am -e -i -u -ey -i; negation نه before the verb; future =
   به + present; past of "to be" وم/و/وه; the ergative past-transitive flip
   (ما ډوډۍ وخوړه — taught gently, recognition first); circumpositions
   په…کې. Numbers/prices use everyday Kabul-style vocabulary; days of the
   week are the Afghan (Persian-loan) names as recognition vocab.
   Content quality is research-verified, not native-reviewed (CLAUDE.md).
   Art: secular Afghanistan — snow-capped Hindu Kush, arid valley terraces,
   poplars and a pomegranate orchard. Mascot: markhor kid (national animal). */

